      "source": [
        "# Callable\n",
        "\n",
        "A callable is an object that can be called using parentheses, such as a function, class, or instance implementing `__call__()`. Use `callable(obj)` to test for callability.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-callable)"
      ]
    }
